---
import UesLivingStudy from '../../../components/UesLivingStudy.astro';
import study from '../../../data/ues-living-studies/death.json';
import models from '../../../data/ues-living-studies/death-models.json';
const navigation=[{href:'#different-questions',label:'01 · QUESTIONS & EVIDENCE',title:'Mortality study'},{href:'#model-expressions',label:'02 · ACTUAL MODEL TEXT',title:'An expression room'},{href:'#edition',label:'03 · DOCUMENTARY DRAFT',title:'Edition & provenance'}];
const artCaption='An empty chair, a folded letter, and afternoon light. Original conceptual artwork about absence and attention; no body or afterlife is depicted.';
---
<UesLivingStudy study={study} author="Michael Hoydich" credit="Research, drafting, and original vector art assistance: Codex" navigation={navigation} navigationLabel="Mortality feature sections" artCaption={artCaption}>
  <Fragment slot="exhibition">
    <section class="study-section expression-room" id="model-expressions" aria-labelledby="expression-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">A SMALL EXHIBITION · TWO ACTUAL RESPONSES</p><h2 id="expression-title">How a model expresses a limit.</h2>
      <p>Two independently queried OpenAI models answered the same prompt on October 3, 2026. Their words offer interpretations to examine. Fluency is no evidence that a model feels grief, has consciousness, or knows what follows death. These contributions are unedited interpretive model text, not clinical guidance or definitions of death. The research above supplies the factual and textual grounding.</p>
      <details class="provenance"><summary>The exact shared prompt</summary><p>{models.commonPrompt}</p><p class="fine">Actual platform identifiers appear below; build versions were not exposed. The complete response and provenance are included in the public study JSON.</p></details>
      <div class="study-cards model-cards">{models.contributions.map(model=><article class="study-card"><p class="eyebrow">{model.provider} · ACTUALLY CONSULTED</p><h3>{model.model}</h3><p class="fine">{model.date} · {model.versionDetail}</p><p>{model.excerpt}</p><details><summary>Read the full contribution</summary>{model.response.split('\n\n').map(paragraph=><p>{paragraph}</p>)}</details></article>)}</div>
      <h3 class="room-subheading">Requested voices still unmade.</h3><p>Sonnet, DeepSeek, Udio, and Midjourney have not contributed to this edition. No substitutes are credited to them. The actual OpenAI texts and the original Codex SVG are labeled by their own sources.</p>
      <div class="study-cards">{models.requestedProviders.map(provider=><article class="study-card"><p class="eyebrow">NOT CONSULTED · {provider.medium}</p><h3>{provider.name}</h3><p>{provider.status}</p></article>)}</div>
      <details class="provenance expression-prompts"><summary>Prepared directions for text, sound, and image</summary>{models.unusedPrompts.map(prompt=><div><h3>{prompt.title}</h3><p>{prompt.text}</p><p class="fine">Unsubmitted prompt. No generated {prompt.medium} or cleared reuse rights are asserted.</p></div>)}</details>
      <p class="fine">Access was checked October 3, 2026. Claude is proprietary. No open-weight runtime or licensed local model was verified; software installation alone establishes neither access nor a model license. No new provider login, purchase, generation charge, or credential transfer was performed.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="study-section" id="edition" aria-labelledby="edition-title"><p class="eyebrow">PRESERVATION · REVIEW BEFORE ISSUANCE</p><h2 id="edition-title">An edition can record a work.</h2><p>A review draft gathers the study, actual model contributions, original artwork, source ledger, and exact-byte hashes. It could document one dated version of this feature. It makes no claim to preserve a person, confer ownership of a memory, or settle an afterlife question.</p><p>The PointCast chain has a locally verified development recording. A public network and production mint adapter for this work are unconfigured. No token has been minted or listed; no wallet has been connected, transaction prepared, signature requested, payment made, or operation broadcast. Price, supply, royalties, wallets, collection, token identifiers, and permanent storage are undecided.</p><p><a href="/editions/death-2026-10-03/concept.json" download>Review the documentary edition concept (JSON)</a> · <a href="/chain">PointCast chain status</a></p><p class="fine">This is a metadata and rights review draft. Source links do not license copies of their articles or translations. The edition includes original summaries, with third-party passages, music, and imagery excluded. An issued token would require separately verified rights, approved terms, pinned bytes, and an owner-reviewed signing path.</p><p class="fine">A companion about grief and daily support is being prepared separately. Its publication is pending.</p></section>
  </Fragment>
</UesLivingStudy>
